<BaseLayout title="About — LOLDrivers">
  <div class="document prose">
    <div class="eyebrow">Community intelligence</div>
    <h1>Living Off The Land Drivers</h1>
    <p>
      LOLDrivers is a community-maintained catalog of vulnerable and malicious
      Windows drivers used by adversaries to bypass security controls. The
      project brings together research, sample metadata, and detection resources
      for defenders.
    </p>
    <h2>The people behind the project</h2>
    <p>
      LOLDrivers grew from Michael Haag's driver research and Jose Hernandez's
      work building the project, with contributions from Nasreddine Bencherchali
      and the wider security community. Thanks also to Florian Roth and Patrick
      Bareiss for their early help.
    </p>
    <h2>Contribute a finding</h2>
    <p>
      Driver records live in YAML in the public repository. Contributions can
      add samples, improve metadata, or link new research and detections.
    </p>
    <div class="resource-links">
      <a href="https://github.com/magicsword-io/LOLDrivers/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md">
